<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Brandon and the Westman towns around it show up near the top of Manitoba's radon surveys. In Health Canada's 2012 survey, 44.3% of the homes tested in the Brandon health region were above 200 Bq/m3, the highest share in either Manitoba or Saskatchewan. The 2024 Cross-Canada survey found 36.1% of the Brandon homes it tested at or above that level, from a small sample of homeowners who chose to test.</p><p>None of that tells you what's in your house. Radon has no colour or smell, and the only way to know your number is a long-term test of at least 91 days in the lowest level you actually live in. If the result comes back high, we put you in touch with an independent C-NRPP certified professional who can look at the house and quote a fix. Call now on (204) 555-0173 if you'd like to talk it through first.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Brandon</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Brandon Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Long-term radon testing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A test of at least 91 days, ideally over a Westman heating season, placed in the lowest lived-in level of your home. The Manitoba government puts long-term kits at between $50 and $100. <a href="/radon-testing/">How testing works</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Radon mitigation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">If your Brandon result is over 200 Bq/m3, a certified mitigation professional can install sub-slab depressurization: a pipe through the basement floor, a fan, and a discharge outside. <a href="/radon-mitigation/">How a system works</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Testing for a home sale</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Buying or selling in Brandon with radon on the table? We explain your testing options and point you to your realtor or lawyer for conditions and holdbacks. <a href="/radon-testing-home-sale/">Radon and real estate</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Fan replacement and system checks</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A noisy fan, a dead fan or a manometer that reads flat usually means the system has stopped pulling air. A certified professional can check it and retest. <a href="/radon-fan-replacement/">Fan problems</a>.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
